# Controllers

## Framework semantics

Controllers coordinate request/response flow, interact with components, and delegate persistence to Tables.

## Required behavior

- Keep actions focused on HTTP/application flow.
- Use request/response objects correctly.
- Avoid substantial persistence/domain logic in controllers.
- Prefer components for reusable controller-level concerns when appropriate.

## Anti-patterns

- Persistence concern in controller
- Fat controller
- Inventing FormRequest-style classes (not Laravel)

## Review checklist

- [ ] Action is orchestration, not a Table replacement
- [ ] Validation/rules live on the model layer where appropriate